{
  "info": {
    "name": "KairoX \u00b7 Dashboard",
    "description": "The per-role manager screens: cutting, lining, stitching, store and the Direct Manager's own. Every one is a read.\n\nSETUP\n  1. Import the whole folder and SELECT the KairoX environment\n     (top-right). That is what shares one token across every\n     collection \u2014 a collection variable is visible only to the\n     collection that set it.\n  2. Run `user` \u2192 Login. Its test script stores `access_token` for\n     you; there is nothing to copy and paste.\n  3. Every request here inherits bearer auth from that token.\n\n`base_url` defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000.\n\nOptional query params are present but DISABLED, so each request runs\nas-is. File uploads are real form-data rows \u2014 click Select Files on\nthe `file` row. Generated from the app's own OpenAPI schema by\n`python scripts/make_postman_per_service.py` \u2014 re-run it after changing\nroutes rather than editing requests by hand.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
